WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.380 --> 00:00:04.680
There's a lot of stuff in Wonder Woman that's
different, not just from the previous DCEU

00:00:04.680 --> 00:00:08.090
films, but from most superhero movies in general
that came before it.

00:00:08.090 --> 00:00:12.470
As a result, it will likely have a lasting
effect on the DCEU, opening doors with regards

00:00:12.470 --> 00:00:13.960
to world-building and narrative.

00:00:14.620 --> 00:00:19.240
Man of Steel was an extremely dark and bloody
take on a traditionally upbeat character,

00:00:19.240 --> 00:00:20.869
to the chagrin of fans and critics.

00:00:20.869 --> 00:00:25.119
Batman v Superman took that even further,
depicting two heroes who are traditionally

00:00:25.120 --> 00:00:27.420
friends as bitterly opposed for most of the
movie.

00:00:27.560 --> 00:00:31.460
Suicide Squad featured super-powered criminals
forced into service by the government, so

00:00:31.460 --> 00:00:33.860
obviously it wasn't sunshine and rainbows
either.

00:00:33.980 --> 00:00:35.820
But Wonder Woman tells a different story.

00:00:36.100 --> 00:00:37.100
It's certainly violent.

00:00:37.640 --> 00:00:41.500
It is a war movie, after all, but it depicts
its title hero as a symbol of hope.

00:00:41.500 --> 00:00:45.050
When she's first revealed in costume, stepping
out into No Man's Land in the midst of the

00:00:45.050 --> 00:00:48.000
Great War, the point is not that she's there
to destroy.

00:00:48.140 --> 00:00:49.920
She's there to save everyone instead.

00:00:50.220 --> 00:00:54.040
In a world where Superman snaps a villain's
neck and Batman brands criminals so they'll

00:00:54.040 --> 00:00:58.170
be killed in prison, Wonder Woman offers a
refreshing return to the basic concept of

00:00:58.170 --> 00:01:02.260
a superhero, moving away from the idea that
traditional heroism has lost its place.

00:01:02.780 --> 00:01:04.160
"It's about what you believe.

00:01:07.800 --> 00:01:09.240
And I believe in love."

00:01:09.440 --> 00:01:13.899
Where Superman is an alien and Batman is a
billionaire with a lot of tech, Wonder Woman

00:01:13.900 --> 00:01:18.060
is a demigod with magical powers who grew
up on an idyllic island wit immortal women.

00:01:18.249 --> 00:01:23.300
Her movie embraces fantasy elements to a degree
that the DCEU really hadn't before.

00:01:23.300 --> 00:01:26.100
It may not be the first DC movie to feature
magic.

00:01:26.289 --> 00:01:29.960
Suicide Squad's villain, after all, is literally
named "the Enchantress."

00:01:29.960 --> 00:01:31.980
But Diana's origin takes it to another level.

00:01:32.140 --> 00:01:36.460
This is a movie that starts out in a purely
fantasy setting before introducing the real

00:01:36.460 --> 00:01:36.960
world.

00:01:36.960 --> 00:01:41.860
Even the MCU presents Asgard as more of a
sci-fi realm in another dimension that merely

00:01:41.860 --> 00:01:43.400
inspired Earth mythology.

00:01:43.560 --> 00:01:46.100
Wonder Woman, however, doesn't hedge its bets
like that.

00:01:46.460 --> 00:01:50.160
Diana grows up in a place that's like an all-female
version of Lord of the Rings.

00:01:50.160 --> 00:01:53.600
That doesn't just shape her abilities; it
also affects her outlook.

00:01:53.820 --> 00:01:57.860
Her reaction to learning about the horrors
of World War I is to go on a quest to defeat

00:01:57.860 --> 00:01:58.580
a mad god.

00:01:58.720 --> 00:02:03.380
She's a superhero to be sure, but she's also
a fantasy character, and that blend is carried

00:02:03.380 --> 00:02:04.080
off perfectly.

00:02:04.389 --> 00:02:08.160
Bringing her into a world that also features
science-based heroes like Cyborg and the Flash

00:02:08.160 --> 00:02:11.370
creates endless possibilities for future stories
in this universe.

00:02:12.360 --> 00:02:17.060
In actual real-world history, Wonder Woman's
first comic book appearance was in 1941.

00:02:17.100 --> 00:02:21.780
However, because comics continuity is constantly
revised to keep everyone young, the version

00:02:21.780 --> 00:02:25.560
of Wonder Woman in the current comics only
left Themyscira roughly ten years ago.

00:02:25.710 --> 00:02:29.420
The movie takes a different path, as this
Diana leaves during World War I, and goes

00:02:29.420 --> 00:02:32.540
on to live in the outside world for about
a hundred years.

00:02:32.560 --> 00:02:36.200
As far as we know, Wonder Woman was the first
superhero in this version of Earth.

00:02:36.440 --> 00:02:40.640
That raises the question: if she's been around
for a century, who else might have shown up

00:02:40.640 --> 00:02:41.380
along the way?

00:02:41.500 --> 00:02:46.760
There's a whole roster of DC Comics characters
from the 1930s and 1940s, and with Wonder

00:02:46.760 --> 00:02:50.340
Woman setting the precedent, it's possible
some of them might've existed even earlier

00:02:50.340 --> 00:02:51.600
in the DCEU.

00:02:51.600 --> 00:02:54.790
While it's unclear if the movies will ever
deal with much of that, the precedent has

00:02:54.790 --> 00:02:59.280
been set, and a 100-year history of superheroes
is rich with possibilities.

00:02:59.680 --> 00:03:03.920
Superheroes tend to be monogamous and mate
for life, especially in movies.

00:03:04.040 --> 00:03:08.100
In that vein, Steve Trevor plays a key role
in Wonder Woman's origin story, so it's no

00:03:08.100 --> 00:03:11.080
surprise he's a big part of the movie, as
played by Chris Pine.

00:03:11.120 --> 00:03:15.060
However, since the film is set a century in
the past, there was never a chance for the

00:03:15.070 --> 00:03:18.180
two to live happily ever after, since she's
immortal and he isn't.

00:03:18.180 --> 00:03:21.820
Ultimately the plot takes it even further,
with Trevor sacrificing his life to destroy

00:03:21.820 --> 00:03:25.480
a plane full of Doctor Poison's gas after
he and Diana kiss.

00:03:25.480 --> 00:03:30.180
For a superhero's lover to die in a movie
is almost unheard of, especially by way of

00:03:30.180 --> 00:03:31.380
a heroic sacrifice.

00:03:31.900 --> 00:03:33.020
"I wish we had more time."

00:03:34.340 --> 00:03:34.840
"What?

00:03:35.120 --> 00:03:36.020
What are you saying?"

00:03:37.640 --> 00:03:38.360
"I love you!"

00:03:40.740 --> 00:03:44.840
In addition to this narrative departure, director
Patty Jenkins has said that Diana will have

00:03:44.840 --> 00:03:46.620
a different love interest in the sequel.

00:03:46.760 --> 00:03:50.880
It'll reportedly be set in the 1980s, which
means that whoever that person is, it will

00:03:50.880 --> 00:03:52.880
also likely only last for one movie.

00:03:52.880 --> 00:03:56.970
Depending on how long this goes on, Diana
could become the first superhero since the

00:03:56.970 --> 00:04:00.660
'80s and '90s-era Batman to have a different
love interest in every movie.

00:04:01.300 --> 00:04:05.720
Wonder Woman's power goes beyond her physical
and mystical capabilities within the movies.

00:04:05.780 --> 00:04:10.320
As a character, she's proven to be more powerful
than anyone expected, and so has her first

00:04:10.320 --> 00:04:10.820
movie.

00:04:11.000 --> 00:04:15.460
The film wasn't just a huge success financially,
it was a hit with critics, a feat managed

00:04:15.460 --> 00:04:17.500
by no previous DCEU movie.

00:04:17.650 --> 00:04:21.560
In the wake of its release, there was a lively
public discussion about how the creative minds

00:04:21.570 --> 00:04:25.270
behind the DCEU had lessons to learn from
Wonder Woman.

00:04:25.270 --> 00:04:27.250
"I want her to be everything for me."

00:04:27.250 --> 00:04:31.020
It was too late to change much about Justice
League, which came out only five months later.

00:04:31.310 --> 00:04:35.400
But going forward it's clear that it's Wonder
Woman, not Superman or Batman, who will light

00:04:35.400 --> 00:04:37.840
the way forward for the DC superhero franchise.

00:04:37.960 --> 00:04:41.260
Until now, Clark and Bruce have spent too
much time fighting in the dark.

00:04:41.500 --> 00:04:45.240
But it already looks like that's changing,
as evidenced by Aquaman and Shazam!, which

00:04:45.240 --> 00:04:49.500
are both brighter and lighter in tone and
color palette than most of what's come before.

